# Decision Logic Diagram

```
Perception Input → State Estimation → Goal Reasoning → Action Selection → Execution
       ↓                ↓                  ↓                ↓             ↓
Sensory Data    Current Situation   Desired Outcomes   Available      Motor
                Uncertainty         Priority Weights   Behaviors      Commands
```

## Description

This diagram shows the decision-making pipeline in humanoid robots, starting with perception inputs that are processed to estimate the current state. The system then reasons about goals and priorities before selecting appropriate actions from available behaviors. The selected actions are then executed as motor commands, with the cycle continuing as new perception data becomes available.